{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W4KpXv7HcPZNthC3fKiJSg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Webhooks\n2\t\n3\tWebhooks were introduced in 2023 after several customers asked for a way to avoid\n4\tpolling. At the time, two designs were discussed, and the push model was chosen because\n5\tpolling was considered wasteful.\n6\t\n7\tIn this guide you will learn everything about webhooks.\n8\t\n9\t## Setup\n10\t\n11\tFirst, the endpoint must be registered. It is done in the dashboard, under\n12\t**Settings > Webhooks**. Simply paste the URL and the events will be delivered.\n13\t\n14\tThe following events exist:\n15\t\n16\t| Event | When |\n17\t|---|---|\n18\t| `invoice.paid` | An invoice is paid |\n19\t| `invoice.failed` | A charge fails |\n20\t| `customer.deleted` | A customer is deleted |\n21\t\n22\tAfter registration a secret is generated. It should be stored safely, because it is\n23\tshown only once.\n24\t\n25\t## Verifying signatures\n26\t\n27\tEach delivery is signed. The signature is sent in the `X-Signature` header and must be\n28\tverified before the payload is trusted. It is computed with HMAC-SHA256 over the raw\n29\tbody.\n30\t\n31\t## Retries\n32\t\n33\tIf a delivery fails, it is retried. After some attempts, the endpoint is disabled and an\n34\temail is sent.\n35\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ac7508c9-4fbc-4df2-a3e6-be6f95a3aeac","uuid":"4d96ad81-51ef-4418-a69c-d6d51279ecad","timestamp":"2026-11-23T15:35:01.395Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-cassiobotaro-Projetos-skills/d0a072a6-567b-4982-98be-0db22c9a4fba/scratchpad/tw-haiku/p24/project/docs/webhooks.md","content":"# Webhooks\n\nWebhooks were introduced in 2023 after several customers asked for a way to avoid\npolling. At the time, two designs were discussed, and the push model was chosen because\npolling was considered wasteful.\n\nIn this guide you will learn everything about webhooks.\n\n## Setup\n\nFirst, the endpoint must be registered. It is done in the dashboard, under\n**Settings > Webhooks**. Simply paste the URL and the events will be delivered.\n\nThe following events exist:\n\n| Event | When |\n|---|---|\n| `invoice.paid` | An invoice is paid |\n| `invoice.failed` | A charge fails |\n| `customer.deleted` | A customer is deleted |\n\nAfter registration a secret is generated. It should be stored safely, because it is\nshown only once.\n\n## Verifying signatures\n\nEach delivery is signed. The signature is sent in the `X-Signature` header and must be\nverified before the payload is trusted. It is computed with HMAC-SHA256 over the raw\nbody.\n\n## Retries\n\nIf a delivery fails, it is retried. After some attempts, the endpoint is disabled and an\nemail is sent.\n","numLines":35,"startLine":1,"totalLines":35}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01W4KpXv7HcPZNthC3fKiJSg","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
