{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011ChL74LQyGorCgRFkzPEK9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed `docs/webhooks.md` (34 lines). The repo contains only this file, so I could not check any claim against code. Everything below is about the prose and what the reader can do after reading it. I did not edit the file.\n\n## Blocking: facts the reader needs that are missing\n\n1. **Signature format is undefined.** The doc says the signature is HMAC-SHA256 over the raw body, sent in `X-Signature`, but not how it is encoded (hex or base64), whether it has a prefix, or whether a timestamp is included. A receiver cannot implement verification from this. Add the exact format and a short verification example.\n2. **Retry policy is vague.** \"After some attempts\" does not say how many attempts, the interval or backoff, or what counts as a failure (non-2xx, timeout, connection error). It also does not say how to re-enable a disabled endpoint, or who receives the email.\n3. **Event list may be incomplete.** \"The following events exist\" reads as a full list. Confirm whether it is complete, and say so if it is not.\n4. **Event names and descriptions don't match.** `invoice.failed` is described as \"A charge fails.\" Either the name or the description is wrong, or the doc needs to explain the relationship between invoices and charges.\n5. **Subscription is unclear.** \"Simply paste the URL and the events will be delivered\" does not say whether the endpoint receives all events or the ones chosen in the table. It also does not give URL requirements (HTTPS, port, redirects).\n6. **No payload example.** A receiver developer needs the JSON shape, including the event ID, type, and timestamp.\n\n## Important: the doc does not match its job\n\n- **The history paragraph** (2023, two designs, polling) is design background, not something a reader needs to set up a webhook. Cut it or move it to a changelog or ADR.\n-